# Cloudflare Pages redirect rules.
#
# This repository is public AND its files are served from the live site, so
# anything committed here is world-readable at a stable URL. The Node test
# suite and the README are development files with no reason to exist on a form
# that families open: /test/consent-form.test.mjs served a real child's name,
# his guardian's name, her email, his town and his book title until 2026-09-01.
#
# The names are gone, but the surface should not be here either. Fewer files
# published is fewer files to get this wrong in again.
#
# Caveat worth knowing if you change this: Pages applies redirects to requests
# that do not match a static asset, so a rule cannot always shadow a file that
# physically exists. If /test/* still returns the file after a deploy, the
# reliable fix is to stop publishing it: a Pages build command of
# `rm -rf test README.md`, or moving the served assets into their own output
# directory. Verify with curl after deploying, never by reading this file.

/test/*      /404 404
/README.md   /404 404
